## What this predicate means

**Agent A `made` memory B** — FOAF agent-creation typed-edge.  The dagger inverse of `created-by` — where `created-by` is the memorial-side assertion ("this memorial was created by Agent X"), `made` is the agent-side assertion ("Agent A made these memorials").  Per `protocol/predicate_lifecycle.md` §"Edge assertion is one-sided", the canonical asserted direction is the memorial side (`created-by:`); `made:` is derivable via inverse-of entailment on the agent side and exists for vocabulary completeness + reverse-direction retrieval.

