## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Asymmetric** — Agent A made memory B doesn't imply memory B made Agent A (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — agents don't "make" themselves (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)
- **NOT transitive**

## When to use made

In typical authoring posture, you DON'T write `made:` on actor memorials.  You write `created-by:` on the artifact memorial (pointing to the actor); the substrate derives `made:` on the actor side via OWL 2 RL `prp-inv1`/`prp-inv2` once `:dt/inverse-of` is declared between the pair.

Use `made:` directly only when authoring an actor-centric retrieval ("show every memorial Dan made via Claude Opus 4.7") — and even then, prefer the inverse query (`/memory-search --inbound-predicate created-by --from actors/dan-lentz.md`).

